The obvious alternative was to split the checking half off instead of the
gathering half, leaving peff-commit to draft and a second skill to
critique. That fails on file layout rather than on principle: drafting
and checking both need PEFF-STYLE.md, so a third copy would exist and
would drift the way peff-review's already has.

The `asked` tag is defined here but never written by this skill, which
asks nothing. Only an interviewing caller sets it. It lives in this
table rather than in peff-commit so that both callers read one list of
tags.
